  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Monday) \nIssued at 1242 PM CDT Tue Sep 15 2026\n\nDry and very warm conditions carry into Friday as a broad ~599 \ndam H5 sets up over AR into northeast TX. Not until Friday night \ndo we see this high faltering which allows monsoonal moisture to \ncreep into our westernmost counties complete with some rain \nchances. The arrival of a improved SW flow aloft on Saturday in \nthe base of a broad trough cresting the Rockies spells improved \nrain chances, especially on the Caprock, where the axis of \nmonsoonal moisture overlaps with a SW-NE surface trough. This \npattern supports a regional precip event with heavy rain at times \ngiven PWAT anomalies reaching +0.5 to +0.8\" and a window for \ntraining convection. The pattern remains unsettled and turns \ncooler for Sunday following a bona fide cold front with reasonably\nmoist E-NE winds in the lowest levels. With southwest flow \nlingering aloft through early next week, additional chances for \nprecip remain intact despite mixed ensemble signals.",
